  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Trusted Agronomist",
    "overview": "Rootology looks and behaves like a good agronomist you trust: sober and precise, it says what it knows, what it does not know and where it knows it from. The interface stays out of the way of the answer; the brand lives in precise details (the sprout in the wordmark, Fraunces in the titles, the line drawings) rather than in decoration.\n\nWithin that sobriety the character is warm and tactile, a thing made for the garden: earthy neutrals that lean towards the green of the sprout, soft rounded shapes, small one-line drawings, comfortable touch targets for a phone held in one hand outdoors. Warmth comes from colour temperature, type and drawings, never from noise.\n\nThe confirmed anti-reference is anything playful or childish: saturated colours, mascots inside the app, the tone of an app for children.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Sprout green is the one accent, used where the person acts.",
      "States have fixed colours and meanings everywhere: frost blue, pest amber, waiting violet, Lumo's success green and error red.",
      "Flat, softly bordered surfaces; depth by tone, not by shadow.",
      "A clear icon with a value or a count rather than a sentence; the word stays as tooltip and aria label.",
      "Fraunces for titles and the wordmark; the system font for everything a person reads quickly."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Rule",
        "body": "Sprout green marks where to act; it is never decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Meaning Rule",
        "body": "A state colour means one thing everywhere: violet is always \"waiting for a person\", amber always a pest, blue always frost.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif-for-Titles Rule",
        "body": "Fraunces appears only in h1–h4, the wordmark and the slogan; never in running text, buttons or fields.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-By-Default Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces are flat at rest; a shadow means something floats above the page.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use sprout green only where the person acts or chooses.",
      "Do keep each state colour to its one meaning, in light and in dark.",
      "Do prefer an icon with a value or a count, with the word as tooltip and aria label.",
      "Do check every screen at 360 px, in dark mode and with a keyboard.",
      "Do keep styles in styles/rootology.css; no inline styles on components."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't make it playful or childish: no saturated palettes, no mascot inside the app, no toy-like shapes.",
      "Don't set running text, buttons or fields in Fraunces.",
      "Don't add shadows to resting cards or decorate with colour.",
      "Don't use \"giardino\" for the vegetable garden: it is \"orto\"."
    ]
  }
}